        "original_id": "e9a8052e-e5fb-5c7c-b0dd-ffbf898f4f38",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Phillip Calvert\n- Places: Province of Maryland, Maryland, North America, Great Britain\n- Roles: Governor of Maryland\n- Concepts: English and British colonies, Thirteen Colonies, U.S. statehood\n\nFacts:\n- The Province of Maryland was founded in 1632 as an English colony in North America.\n- Phillip Calvert, also known as Philip Calvert, was born in 1626.\n- Phillip Calvert was the fifth Governor of Maryland during a brief period in 1660 or 1661.\n- The Province of Maryland later became a British colony.\n- In 1776, the Province of Maryland joined the other twelve of the Thirteen Colonies in rebellion against Great Britain.\n- In 1776, the Province of Maryland became the U.S. state of Maryland.\n- Phillip Calvert died in 1682.",
